 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "should / shouldn't · Why don't you…?",
   "en": "should / shouldn't · Why don't you…?"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "조언은 should / shouldn't + 동사 원형으로 합니다. 모든 주어에 같은 형태입니다. 부드럽게 제안할 때는 Why don't you + 동사 원형?도 많이 씁니다. 조언을 구할 때는 What should I do?라고 합니다.",
   "en": "Give advice with should / shouldn't + base verb. It is the same for every subject. A friendly way to suggest something is 'Why don't you + base verb?'. To ask for advice say 'What should I do?'."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Form",
    "예문 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "should + 동사",
     "You should rest."
    ],
    [
     "shouldn't + 동사",
     "You shouldn't work today."
    ],
    [
     "Should I + 동사?",
     "Should I see a doctor?"
    ],
    [
     "Why don't you + 동사?",
     "Why don't you try some tea?"
    ],
    [
     "What should I do?",
     "I'm stressed. What should I do?"
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "should 뒤에는 동사 원형: You should go (✕ should to go).",
    "en": "After should use the base verb: You should go (not should to go)."
   },
   {
    "ko": "should는 must보다 약한 조언입니다.",
    "en": "Should is weaker than must; it is advice, not a rule."
   },
   {
    "ko": "I think you should ~는 더 부드러운 말투입니다.",
    "en": "'I think you should ~' sounds softer."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
   {
    "t": "You should see a doctor.",
    "ko": "당신은 의사를 만나는 게 좋아요."
   },
   {
    "t": "You shouldn't go to bed too late.",
    "ko": "너무 늦게 자지 않는 게 좋아요."
   },
   {
    "t": "Why don't you have a rest?",
    "ko": "좀 쉬는 게 어때요?"
   },
   {
    "t": "You should exercise every day.",
    "ko": "매일 운동하는 게 좋아요."
   },
   {
    "t": "What should I do?",
    "ko": "제가 뭘 해야 할까요?"
   }
  ],
